1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,444
A tiny spark. A moving piston. A car pulling away.

2
00:00:04,444 --> 00:00:08,000
Let’s open this engine and connect the dots.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,615
First, lift the covers. Above the cylinders sit two camshafts.

4
00:00:12,615 --> 00:00:17,231
Along the end, a chain links them to the crankshaft.

5
00:00:17,231 --> 00:00:20,000
Below, the sump holds the oil.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,211
Now pull the assemblies apart. Covers, cylinder head, pistons, crankshaft:

7
00:00:24,211 --> 00:00:28,421
each has a place. Look between the big pieces. Those

8
00:00:28,421 --> 00:00:32,632
thin gaskets and small bearings are just as important. This

9
00:00:32,632 --> 00:00:36,000
is an exploded explanation, not a repair sequence.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Pick one piston and look closer. Its crown receives the

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
force from expanding gas. The skirt helps guide its travel

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
inside the cylinder. A small component, carrying a remarkable load.

13
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,545
Bring the pieces home. The head seals the cylinders, the

14
00:00:52,545 --> 00:00:57,091
covers close the engine, and the mechanism is ready to

15
00:00:57,091 --> 00:00:58,000
move again.

16
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,103
Watch the connecting rods follow the crankpins. Each piston moves

17
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:06,205
up and down, while the crankshaft turns. The cylinders take

18
00:01:06,205 --> 00:01:10,308
turns firing: one, three, four, two. Their power strokes keep

19
00:01:10,308 --> 00:01:14,000
handing the motion from one cylinder to the next.

20
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,242
Zoom in on the timing chain. In this four-stroke engine,

21
00:01:18,242 --> 00:01:22,485
the crankshaft turns twice for every camshaft revolution. The cam

22
00:01:22,485 --> 00:01:26,727
lobes open the valves; springs close them. Timing makes the

23
00:01:26,727 --> 00:01:28,000
whole sequence possible.

24
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,889
Follow the cyan air through the intake. The throttle controls

25
00:01:31,889 --> 00:01:35,778
the opening, and the intake valves admit the fresh charge.

26
00:01:35,778 --> 00:01:39,667
Pink traces the fuel paths. Air and fuel must meet

27
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:42,000
before combustion can do useful work.

28
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,286
Let’s slow down and stay with one cylinder. Intake draws

29
00:01:46,286 --> 00:01:50,571
the fresh charge in. Compression squeezes it. Near the top,

30
00:01:50,571 --> 00:01:54,857
the spark begins combustion. Expanding gas pushes the piston down:

31
00:01:54,857 --> 00:01:59,143
the power stroke. Finally, exhaust clears the cylinder for the

32
00:01:59,143 --> 00:02:00,000
next cycle.

33
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,138
The exhaust valve opens and the rising piston pushes spent

34
00:02:04,138 --> 00:02:08,276
gas out. Follow the violet path toward the exhaust manifold.

35
00:02:08,276 --> 00:02:12,000
Then the next intake stroke starts the cycle again.

36
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,186
Now switch to the amber oil circuit. The pump draws

37
00:02:16,186 --> 00:02:20,372
oil from the sump and sends it through the filter.

38
00:02:20,372 --> 00:02:24,558
Galleries carry it to the bearings and cylinder head. The

39
00:02:24,558 --> 00:02:28,744
oil film reduces contact between moving surfaces before the oil

40
00:02:28,744 --> 00:02:30,000
drains back down.

41
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,444
Combustion also produces heat. Follow the blue coolant around the

42
00:02:34,444 --> 00:02:38,889
cylinders and through the head. While the engine is cold,

43
00:02:38,889 --> 00:02:43,333
the bypass keeps coolant circulating. As it warms, the thermostat

44
00:02:43,333 --> 00:02:47,778
opens the radiator route. Heat can then pass from the

45
00:02:47,778 --> 00:02:50,000
coolant into the surrounding air.

46
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,889
Pull back and close the covers. The engine works because

47
00:02:53,889 --> 00:02:57,778
its systems work together: timed motion, a fresh charge, combustion,

48
00:02:57,778 --> 00:03:01,667
lubrication and cooling. We have slowed and simplified their behavior

49
00:03:01,667 --> 00:03:04,000
so you can see the relationships.

50
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,211
But what changes when you move the throttle? That part

51
00:03:08,211 --> 00:03:12,421
is yours to explore. Open How Things Click, rotate the

52
00:03:12,421 --> 00:03:16,632
engine, remove a part, and trace the flows yourself. The

53
00:03:16,632 --> 00:03:20,000
link to the interactive is in the description.
